; C11  Winning 42 pp. 25-26 (W42-p025-f, W42-p026-a), p. 11 (W42-p011-b),
; p. 24 (W42-p024-a, the boundary); played in Hands 28 and 30 (pp. 99, 105)
; Rule, in our words: with trump drawn, a bidder holding an off and the double
; of the off's suit leads the double first; it may pull the count the off
; would lose. A double of another suit does not count.
; Python gate (pour_bidder gate_c11): bidder on lead, no trump outside his
; hand, a non-trump double and an off of the same suit; the book's tiles are
; such doubles.
; How this encoding differs: it cannot say "no trump outside the hand" and
; fires with trump still out. In Hand 30 (p. 105) the book plays this rule with
; the last trump in the partner's hand, where the gate does not fire.
; GAP declarer: the bidder is written in as S0.
; GAP none: "trumps drawn" is "no live trump outside the hand", a negated
; existential.
(policy c11-double-ahead-of-the-off
  (initial play)
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule lead-the-double (in play) (next play) (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (domino doubled) (domino off) (domino over) (context suit))
        (out doubled)
        (pattern
          (viewer S0)
          (leader S0)
          (next-actor S0)
          ; GAP none: (none (live t) (in t q*) (not (own-legal t)))
          (own-legal doubled)
          (double doubled)
          (not (in doubled q*))
          (leads-context doubled suit)
          (own-legal off)
          (in off suit)
          (live over)
          (not (own-legal over))
          (in over suit)
          (beats over off suit))))))
